WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.667
Matthew, Chapter Twenty-Two.

2
00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:18.267
And Jesus answered and spake unto them again by parables, and said, The kingdom of heaven is like unto a certain king, which made a marriage for his son, And sent forth his servants to call them that were bidden to the wedding: and they would not come.

3
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:29.200
Again, he sent forth other servants, saying, Tell them which are bidden, Behold, I have prepared my dinner: my oxen and my fatlings are killed, and all things are ready: come unto the marriage.

4
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:38.667
But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his merchandise: And the remnant took his servants, and entreated them spitefully, and slew them.

5
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:46.133
But when the king heard thereof, he was wroth: and he sent forth his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city.

6
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:51.867
Then saith he to his servants, The wedding is ready, but they which were bidden were not worthy.

7
00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:57.333
Go ye therefore into the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage.

8
00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:05.733
So those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they found, both bad and good: and the wedding was furnished with guests.

9
00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:16.800
And when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding garment: And he saith unto him, Friend, how camest thou in hither not having a wedding garment?

10
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.133
And he was speechless.

11
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:27.867
Then said the king to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and take him away, and cast him into outer darkness; there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.

12
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:31.333
For many are called, but few are chosen.

13
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:36.400
Then went the Pharisees, and took counsel how they might entangle him in his talk.

14
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:50.133
And they sent out unto him their disciples with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, neither carest thou for any man: for thou regardest not the person of men.

15
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.400
Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou?

16
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.000
Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?

17
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.333
But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said, Why tempt ye me, ye hypocrites?

18
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.800
Shew me the tribute money.

19
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.933
And they brought unto him a penny.

20
00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:08.533
And he saith unto them, Whose is this image and superscription?

21
00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:11.333
They say unto him, Caesar's.

22
00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:19.067
Then saith he unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things which are Caesar's; and unto God the things that are God's.

23
00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:24.000
When they had heard these words, they marvelled, and left him, and went their way.

24
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:38.133
The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and asked him, Saying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.

25
00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:52.400
Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife, deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother: Likewise the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.

26
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.400
And last of all the woman died also.

27
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.533
Therefore in the resurrection whose wife shall she be of the seven?

28
00:02:58.533 --> 00:03:00.533
for they all had her.

29
00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:07.333
Jesus answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.

30
00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:14.267
For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven.

31
00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:24.800
But as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken unto you by God, saying, I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?

32
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.400
God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.

33
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.267
And when the multitude heard this, they were astonished at his doctrine.

34
00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:37.733
But when the Pharisees had heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, they were gathered together.

35
00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:46.133
Then one of them, which was a lawyer, asked him a question, tempting him, and saying, Master, which is the great commandment in the law?

36
00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:54.267
Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.

37
00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.267
This is the first and great commandment.

38
00:03:56.267 --> 00:04:01.067
And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.

39
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:05.067
On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.

40
00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:10.533
While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them, Saying, What think ye of Christ?

41
00:04:10.533 --> 00:04:11.733
whose son is he?

42
00:04:11.733 --> 00:04:13.867
They say unto him, The Son of David.

43
00:04:13.867 --> 00:04:24.800
He saith unto them, How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying, The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool?

44
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.133
If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?

45
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:35.067
And no man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask him any more questions.

